<title>USA: Texas $2.9 billion TRANs won by 16 firms.</title>
<headline>Texas $2.9 billion TRANs won by 16 firms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sixteen firms won portions of the $2.9 billion of Texas 1996 tax and revenue anticipation note offering on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Over 50 bids totaling over $9 billion were submitted for the competively auctioned notes.  </p>
<p>    FIRM		AMOUNT			NIC</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>BT Securities	$325,000,000		3.9876</p>
<p>Bank of America    $105,000,000		3.9577</p>
<p>Bear Sterans	 $150,000,000		3.9999</p>
<p>Citicorp	     $200,000,000		4.0001</p>
<p>Dillion Read	 $15,000,000		 3.9999</p>
<p>First Albany Corp  $75,000,000		 4.0049</p>
<p>First Chicago	$210,00,000		 3.9508</p>
<p>First Southwest    $92,100,000		 4.0045</p>
<p>JC Bradford	  $10,000,000		 3.9979</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers    $350,000,000		3.9963</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch	$247,000,000		4.0121</p>
<p>Nat City	     $10,000,000		 4.0054</p>
<p>PaineWebber	  $320,000,000		4.0005</p>
<p>Prudential	   $25,000,000		 3.9908</p>
<p>Smith Barney	 $700,000,000		4.0042</p>
<p>Zions Bank	   $66,000,000		 4.0052</p>
<p>The aggregate net interest cost (NIC) was 3.99619755921 percent.</p>
<p>The state said a total of 72 bods were submitted totaling $9.9 billion.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
